      "facts": [
        "Legacy older-server refusal, retained by SDK/CLI/Web recovery handlers. Current servers use session pacing and no longer emit this spend cutoff.",
        "Historical per-model ceilings, retained as soft session pacing targets. Crossing a target adds a pause; it never refuses a prompt or model call.",
        "Optional model-specific pacing target; the legacy name is retained.",
        "Freebucks meters access through session prices and a daily pool, while session length and per-session pacing govern usage within an hour.",
        "Compatibility notices, not spend enforcement. Completions uses the capacity/restricted notices for live request-rate limits. The local Freebucks stub and legacy refusal mapping retain the older copy."
