      "facts": [
        "Whether the one-time Freebucks introduction is on screen, and how to retire it.",
        "The card itself, above the picker on the landing. Rendered only while `useFreebucksIntro` says its state is visible; it is a card and not a modal because the CLI landing has no modal layer.",
        "It owns the dismissal key and consumes it, see the hook above for why that is one of two guards rather than the only one.",
        "The intro card owns the keyboard while it is up: its \"press any key\" must not also commit the focused row.",
        "Ignore every key while something above the picker owns the keyboard. The Freebucks intro card is the one caller: it says \"press any key to continue\", and without this the same key also committed the focused row and charged for a session the user never picked."
      ],
      "title": "CLI update: freebucks-intro-card",
      "summary": "CLI changes across 3 file(s) (+386/−79).",
      "tags": [
        "cli"
      ],
      "day": "2026-09-08",
      "month": "2026-09",
      "category": "CLI",
      "significance": "notable",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Fix Freebucks intro keypress charging for an unpaid session",
        "summary": "The FreebucksIntroCard now stops the dismissal key from propagating, and the landing screen suspends the model picker's keyboard while the intro is visible, so the same key press no longer both dismisses the card and commits a focused row on the cheapest model. A new `useFreebucksIntro` hook centralizes visibility, and `FreebuffModelSelector` gained a `keyboardSuspended` prop that gates its `useKeyboard` handler plus an `isPressable`/`isPricedOut` path that opens the plans page for rows the balance cannot cover. This closes the most reported Freebucks bug where pressing any key on the intro started a session for a model the user did not choose.",
        "significance": "major",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/components/freebucks-intro-card.tsx`, the card's keyboard handler now calls `key.stopPropagation?.()` and `key.preventDefault?.()` before invoking `onDismiss()`, and a new `useFreebucksIntro` hook is exported that owns visibility state. In `cli/src/components/freebuff-landing-screen.tsx`, the landing screen passes `keyboardSuspended={freebucksIntro.visible}` into `<FreebuffModelSelector>`. In `cli/src/components/freebuff-model-selector.tsx`, a new `keyboardSuspended` prop short-circuits `useKeyboard` and a new `isPressable`/`isPricedOut` path lets priced-out rows open the plans page instead of being inert.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "high",
        "verify": "passed",
